			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Route notification, lifecycle, git, nativeHost, and configuration commands through routers\n\nRemove the remaining inline match arms for `notification:*`, `lifecycle:*`, `git:*`, `nativeHost:*`, and `configuration:*` commands from DispatchMatch.rs and route them through their dedicated Router modules. New prefix-based guards also handle `storage:*` and `git:*` Cocoon-forward gates alongside the existing `nativeHost:*` forward path.\n\nStorage/Router.rs gains three new handlers: `storage:optimize` (flushes pending debounced writes to disk), `storage:isUsed`, `storage:close`, and `storage:onDidChangeItems`/`storage:logStorage` (emit `sky://storage/changed` events). The router's route() signature now also takes an `ApplicationHandle` parameter for event emission.\n\nInfo.plist enables debug inspection (`Inspect=1`), recording (`Record=1`), and all-trace logging (`Trace=all`), and adds the `TierShim=None` feature flag.\n\nPunctuation normalization across Debug/Router.rs and DispatchMatch.rs replaces em-dashes with standard hyphens in doc comments.",
			"SHA": "f9c024782e717a9e4edba9d61008df0f373264cf"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-13T00:07:02Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1910,
				41
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Extract Configuration, Debug, Git, Lifecycle, NativeHost, Notification, and Storage routers from monolithic dispatch\n\nReplace inline match arms in DispatchMatch.rs for seven command namespaces with dedicated router modules, each owning its command-to-handler mapping:\n\n- **Configuration/Router.rs** — routes `configuration:*`, `environment:get`, and `workbench:getConfiguration` commands, including the `configuration:inspect` multi-scope inspection with fallback to merged value lookup and the `configuration:onDidChange` channel-listener ack.\n- **Debug/Router.rs** — routes `debug:*` commands with Mountain-native pre-processing (breakpoint storage via ApplicationState, lifecycle event emission to Sky, Debug.Start effect registration) before forwarding to Cocoon via gRPC, or serving breakpoints locally.\n- **Git/Router.rs** — delegates all `git:*` IPC commands (`exec`, `clone`, `pull`, `checkout`, `revParse`, `fetch`, `revListCount`, `cancel`, `isAvailable`) to their existing atom handlers.\n- **Lifecycle/Router.rs** — routes `lifecycle:advancePhase`/`setPhase` (with hidden-until-ready window reveal on phase 3), `getPhase`, `whenPhase`, and `requestShutdown` commands.\n- **NativeHost/Router.rs** — routes the full `nativeHost:*` command surface (~70 commands) spanning dialogs, OS info, window state, clipboard, process/network, power management, and auxiliary window stubs.\n- **Notification/Router.rs** — routes `notification:show`, `showProgress`, `updateProgress`, and `endProgress` to the UI notification atoms.\n- **Storage/Router.rs** — routes `storage:get`, `set`, `getItems`, `updateItems`, `delete`, and `keys` with workspace/global scope discrimination.\n\nEach router returns `Option<Result<Value, String>>` for safe fallthrough, isolating command namespaces into self-contained modules alongside their `mod.rs` declarations. This shrinks the monolithic DispatchMatch.rs match block significantly and makes future additions local to their namespace without touching the central dispatch chain.",
			"SHA": "5846997ff66c8a7b1a5d3c7e7374c49e82c1bbc2"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T23:40:44Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1877,
				10
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Extract Keybinding, Label, and Themes routers from monolithic dispatch\n\nReplace the inline match arms for `keybinding:*`, `label:*`, and `themes:*` commands in `DispatchMatch.rs` with dedicated router modules, following the established pattern already used by `HistoryRouter`. Each new module (`Keybinding/Router.rs`, `Label/LabelRouter.rs`, `Themes/Router.rs`) owns its command-to-handler mapping, routes through the existing UI/Navigation atoms, and returns `Option<Result<Value, String>>` for safe fallthrough.\n\nAlso relay four `tests.*` notification channels through `RelayToSky` in the gRPC service dispatcher, forwarding test lifecycle events (controller_created, run_started, run_ended, result) to the Sky webview via the `sky://tests/*` URI scheme.\n\nThe monolithic `DispatchMatch.rs` match block shrinks by ~50 lines and each command namespace now lives alongside its own module declaration in `mod.rs`, making future additions self-contained without touching the central dispatch chain.",
			"SHA": "f2eedba61768946d226f4440756c218af722cd04"
		},
